2013-11-20 01:29 — Jonadab the Unsightly One:
> On Tuesday, November 19, 2013 7:24:41 AM UTC-5, ais523 wrote:
>>> - When my character was XP 1, she found a kitten on level 3. 
>>> - She also found a gray ooze on level 3.
>> These are both symptoms of a change from NitroHack that I'm not sure
>> about, which makes the character's level have no effect on monster
>> generation. 
> I'm not sure about that one either.  My instinct suggests
> going in the opposite direction, and taking into account
> not only the player's XP level but also his attributes,
> such as strength and (naked) AC.
That would reduce the incentive to level up, look for good gear, and
generally exercise your stats.  I'm not at all sure whether that's a
good idea.

Monster generation based on dungeon level seems not only more realistic
to me (a well-designed level wouldn't “know” when the player enters it),
but also requires the player to find valid strategies for each role to
deal with situations of (in a known way) increasing difficulty the
deeper one explores.

